# Pure DTO Contracts

Types under the project's `Gameplay/Contracts/` folder are the **wire contract** — the serialized shape exchanged with the backend. They must stay **pure data**. Do not add client-side, presentation, or app-specific logic to them.

## Allowed in contracts

- Serialized fields with `[JsonProperty(...)]` (and `[Serializable]`, enum `[EnumMember(...)]`)
- Enum definitions and their wire-name attributes
- XML doc comments and `[JsonIgnore]` on serialization-only concerns

## Not allowed in contracts

Put these on a **client system** (helper method, extension, or static utility in Core/Gameplay/Presentation) instead:

- Display/formatting logic — labels, hierarchy names, UI strings (`DisplayName`, `ToLabel()`)
- Derived presentation values — colors, sprites, icons, sort keys for UI
- Client-only computed properties encoding app behavior rather than wire shape
- Any reference to `UnityEngine.UI`, TMP, sprites, materials, or scene objects

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — client-side label logic on the contract
// Contracts/Domain/Card.cs
public string DisplayName => Value switch { CardValue.Wild => "Wild", _ => $"{Color}_{Value}" };

// ✅ GOOD — private helper on the caller
// Presentation/CardUI/CardFactory.cs
private static string FormatCardName(Card card) => card.Value switch
{
    CardValue.Wild => "Wild",
    _ => $"{card.Color}_{card.Value}",
};
```

## Gray area: wire-derived helpers

Small `[JsonIgnore]` helpers that only restate the wire data (e.g. `Card.IsWild` — fixed by game rules, not the client) are tolerated as part of the data definition. If the value depends on **how the client presents or names things**, it belongs on a client system.

## Changing the contract

When adding or changing wire types, match the backend spec exactly (field names, casing, optionality) and update only the contract folder — mapping/enrichment happens in gameplay systems, not in the DTO.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] No display/formatting/UI logic added to contract types
- [ ] Derived label/visual helpers live on a client system, not the DTO
- [ ] Contract types reference no presentation namespaces or Unity UI types
- [ ] New computed members reflect wire/game data, not client presentation choices
